\end{align*}

Clearly, $f(x)-g(x)=0$ when $\log _{10} x=0$, so $x=1$ is a solution.  Also, $f(x)-g(x)=0$ when $\left(\log _{10} x\right)^{2}=4$, so $\log _{10} x=2$ and $x=10^{2}=100$ is a solution.

